.TH DANBY-LAKEPOLLUTION 1
.SH NAME
danby-lakepollution \- pollutant mass balance in a well-mixed lake
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/lakepollution
.SH MODEL
C' = I/V-(Q/V+k)C.
.PP
C is concentration, I pollutant mass input per unit time, V lake volume,
Q clean-water outflow, and k first-order removal or decay.  The equilibrium
C*=I/(Q+kV) and flushing time 1/(Q/V+k) separate the eventual pollution level
from the speed at which it is approached.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the concentration bar.  Tracks set input mass, volume, outflow, and decay.
Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH NUMERICS
The analytic mass-balance equilibrium is checked by
.B temple/danbytest.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/plugin/lakepollution.b
.br
.B /appl/danby/lakepollution.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR populationmodel (2),
.IR numerics (2)
